---
import EditorialFrame from '../../components/EditorialFrame.astro';
import { records, services, fmtDate } from '../../lib/data.js';
import { newestDate } from '../../lib/editorial.js';

const rec = records.find(record => record.id === 'ca-visitor-visa--in');
const service = services.CA.get('visitor-visa');
const comparisons = ['IN', 'PH', 'PK', 'NG', 'CN', 'BD']
  .map(code => service.records.find(record => record.applicant_country === code))
  .filter(Boolean);
const officialGuide = 'https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/services/application/check-processing-times.html';
---
<EditorialFrame
  sectionName="Guides"
  sectionPath="/guides/"
  slug="canada-visitor-visa-from-india"
  title={`Canada visitor visa processing time from India: ${rec.value_raw} (${fmtDate(rec.effective_date)})`}
  description={`IRCC’s current visitor-visa time from India, what the clock includes, how India compares and why post-biometrics anecdotes are a different measure.`}
  h1="Canada visitor visa processing time from India"
  lede={`IRCC currently reports ${rec.value_raw} for visitor-visa applications submitted from India. The number covers the official processing clock, including biometrics time, but does not reserve a decision date for an individual traveler.`}
  modified={newestDate('2026-08-23', rec.effective_date)}
  checked={rec.effective_date}
  about={['Canada visitor visa', 'India', 'IRCC processing times']}
  citations={[officialGuide, rec.source_url]}
  adPrefix="guide-visitor-india"
>
  <div class="stats"><div><div class="n">{rec.value_raw}</div><div class="l">India right now</div></div><div><div class="n">{Math.round(service.medianDays)} days</div><div class="l">published-country median</div></div><div><div class="n">{rec.speed.label}</div><div class="l">relative to the current median</div></div></div>

  <h2>The official clock versus the travel calendar</h2>
  <p>IRCC’s clock starts when it receives a complete application and ends at the decision. Its current guidance says biometrics time is included. The clock does not include the days spent preparing before submission, and a decision is not the same as being ready to travel in every situation.</p>
  <p>That distinction matters because many search results describe “time after biometrics.” IRCC does not publish the India figure on that basis. Applicant reports can be useful personal stories, but they cannot be compared directly with the official complete-application-to-decision statistic.</p>

  <h2>India compared with other large visitor-visa routes</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Applying from</th><th>Current official time</th><th>Relative to median</th></tr></thead><tbody>{comparisons.map(item => (<tr><td><a href={`/canada/visitor-visa/${item.applicantSlug}/`}>{item.applicant_country_name}</a></td><td>{item.value_raw}</td><td>{item.speed?.label || '—'}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Different country times describe different recent inventories and processing conditions. They do not establish that one nationality is more likely to be approved.</p>

  <h2>How much confidence should you put in {rec.value_raw}?</h2>
  <p>Use it as the best official planning estimate available on the data date. Do not treat it as a deadline, and do not subtract days from it to infer an internal application stage. IRCC lists completeness, verification, response time, volume and case complexity among factors that can change the actual wait.</p>
  <div class="callout warn"><strong>Travel planning:</strong> the UK and Canadian government guidance alike warns against treating a processing estimate as a booking guarantee. Verify the official source immediately before making a commitment that is expensive to change.</div>

  <h2>Watch the route, not a screenshot</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/canada/visitor-visa/from-india/">India visitor-visa page</a> carries the current source date and will add a history row when IRCC changes the value. The <a href="/guides/canada-visitor-visa-by-country/">country comparison</a> shows the wider distribution, while the <a href="/reports/canada-processing-time-changes/">Canada report</a> distinguishes a baseline from a verified change.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <h3>Is the India figure based on citizenship?</h3><p>It is selected by the country from which the application is submitted. Citizenship and application location can differ.</p>
  <h3>Does a request for more documents fit inside the estimate?</h3><p>The published figure is an aggregate planning measure. An individual request, verification step or delay responding can make a case take longer.</p>
  <div class="prov">Official source: <a href={officialGuide} rel="noopener">IRCC current processing times</a> and <a href={rec.source_url} rel="noopener">IRCC data</a> · data date {fmtDate(rec.effective_date)}.</div>
</EditorialFrame>
